 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532540,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the area of the regular pentagon with the apothem equal to 5.5 cm and the side length equal to 7 cm.\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/7def413c9fa97b49.png\" alt=\"A pentagon. Each side measures 7 centimeters. The apothem is marked 5.5 centimeters.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The apothem of a regular polygon is a line segment that starts at the center and is perpendicular to a side. The area of a regular polygon with apothem <i>a</i> and perimeter <i>p</i> is <span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap\"></span>.</p>\n<p>A regular pentagon has five sides of equal length. Therefore, the perimeter of a regular pentagon with a side length of 7 cm is:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p = 5(7{\\rm{\\ cm)  =  35\\ cm}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\frac{1}{2}ap = \\frac{1}{2}\\left( {5.5{\\rm{\\ cm}}} \\right)\\left( {35{\\rm{\\ cm}}} \\right) = 96.25{\\rm{\\ c}}{{\\rm{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>The area is 96.25 square centimeters.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"A = 96.25\\,{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\">A = 96.25\\,{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
